# What an appliance carries is the archive of a commit: the tarball the self-update downloads, and
# what xgs-image-builder puts into an image (its fetch-project.sh takes `git archive`). Nothing an
# appliance does not read goes into it: the documentation and its pictures, the workflows, the files
# about the project itself, and the repository's own tools, which run from a checkout here and in
# CI (2026-10-22). A file an appliance starts to read leaves this list in the same change.
# ar_SA.po is the source OPNsense.mo is compiled from; an appliance installs the .mo. i18n/ and
# GLOSSARY.md are the translation's terminology, for whoever translates.
docs/ export-ignore
.github/ export-ignore
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md export-ignore
CONTRIBUTING.md export-ignore
SECURITY.md export-ignore
tools/ export-ignore
i18n/ export-ignore
GLOSSARY.md export-ignore
ar_SA.po export-ignore
.code-language-ignore export-ignore
.private-data-ignore export-ignore
